{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,17]],"date-time":"2026-10-17T16:30:28Z","timestamp":1792254628488,"version":"4.4.0"},"reference-count":32,"publisher":"Institution of Engineering and Technology (IET)","issue":"5","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,18]],"date-time":"2023-10-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1697587200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["62122014"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["62122014"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["62173036"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["62173036"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["ietresearch.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["IET Control Theory &amp; Appl"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,3]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>In this paper, the trajectory tracking problem of controlling a constrained quadrotor with unmeasurable system states in an environment with stochastic wind\u2010gust disturbance is considered. The mathematical model of the quadrotor is divided into the translational system and the rotational system, while only the measurement output of the quadrotor can be accessed. A new output\u2010based control method is developed for solving this problem. In the translational control system, an output feedback stochastic model predictive control (MPC) algorithm is proposed to generate the optimal control sequence with less conservativeness, by taking into account the information on the distribution of the disturbances and the uncertainty resulting from the attitude tracking error. The closed\u2010loop probabilistic constraints satisfaction, the recursive feasibility and the stability of the algorithm are further proved. In the rotational system, the active disturbance rejection control (ADRC) method to estimate and compensate for external disturbances is leveraged and robust control for attitude tracking is accomplished. The convergence of the disturbance estimator and the stability proof are provided. Finally, the robustness and effectiveness of the proposed control strategy are verified by an illustrative\u00a0example.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1049\/cth2.12588","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,19]],"date-time":"2023-10-19T02:57:20Z","timestamp":1697684240000},"page":"566-580","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":6,"title":["Output feedback stochastic MPC for tracking control of quadrotors with disturbances"],"prefix":"10.1049","volume":"18","author":[{"given":"Ruochen","family":"Xue","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Beijing Institute of Technology Beijing China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7268-7548","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Li","family":"Dai","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Beijing Institute of Technology Beijing China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Peizhan","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Beijing Institute of Technology Beijing China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zhongqi","family":"Sun","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Beijing Institute of Technology Beijing China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5977-4911","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yuanqing","family":"Xia","seque